## Math Engine MathML

The mathml math engine converts an explicit TeX subset directly to Presentation MathML with the
pure Ruby implementation bundled with kramdown. It needs no browser, JavaScript runtime, external
TeX executable, or additional gem.

The supported subset contains:

* braces for groups and nested expressions
* subscripts, superscripts, and primes
* frac, dfrac, tfrac, sqrt, and indexed roots
* common Greek letters, operators, relations, arrows, functions, spacing, and symbols
* literal delimiters, left/right, middle, and big-style delimiters
* the matrix, pmatrix, bmatrix, Bmatrix, vmatrix, and Vmatrix environments
* text and the common math/text style commands

Macros are never expanded and no external TeX implementation is invoked. Unsupported commands,
environments, and characters remain errors. The error includes the source position as line,
column, and zero-based offset instead of silently deleting the formula part. By default the error
is rendered in a valid merror element; use math_engine_opts with errors set to :raise to raise
Kramdown::Converter::MathEngine::MathML::ParseError instead.
